---
import { PAGES } from "../content/pages";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Container from "../components/ui/Container.astro";
import Section from "../components/ui/Section.astro";
import Badge from "../components/ui/Badge.astro";
import HelpContacts from "../components/ui/HelpContacts.astro";
import { SITE } from "../content/site";

const linkClass =
  "text-purple-700 underline underline-offset-4 font-bold rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-3 focus-visible:outline-purple-700 focus-visible:outline-offset-2";
---

<BaseLayout meta={PAGES.privacy}>
  <Section variant="surface" class="pt-8 sm:pt-12 pb-16">
    <Container>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
        <div>
          <Badge variant="tint" class="mb-4">Your privacy</Badge>
          <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-green-900 mb-4 leading-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-ink leading-relaxed">
            This policy explains how {SITE.legalName} collects, uses, stores and shares your personal information, and how we
            follow the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs).
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-2">Last updated: November 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-[12px] bg-surface-tint border border-green-200">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-2">The short version</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-ink">
            <li>We only collect information we need to give you safe, good supports.</li>
            <li>We keep it private and secure.</li>
            <li>We only share it when you agree, or when the law says we must.</li>
            <li>You can ask to see your information, or ask us to fix it.</li>
            <li>You can complain to us, or to the Australian privacy regulator (the OAIC).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="text-ink text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-8">
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">1. Who we are</h2>
            <p>
              {SITE.legalName} (ABN {SITE.abn}) is a registered NDIS provider (registration {SITE.ndisRegistration}). We
              support NDIS participants, and we also hold information about their families, carers, nominees and our staff.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">2. What information we collect</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
              <li>Your name, date of birth and contact details.</li>
              <li>Your NDIS number, how your plan is managed, and the supports in your plan.</li>
              <li>
                Health and disability information, such as your support needs, medical or allied health reports, emergency
                contacts and behaviour support plans. This is <strong>sensitive information</strong>, and we only collect it
                with your consent or when the law allows.
              </li>
              <li>Your language, culture and the routines that matter to you.</li>
              <li>Notes about the supports we provide, incident reports, and feedback or complaints.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              When you use the enquiry form on this website, we collect the details you type in. We do not use advertising
              or tracking cookies on this website.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">3. Why we collect it</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
              <li>To answer your enquiry and work out whether we can support you.</li>
              <li>To make a service agreement with you and plan your supports.</li>
              <li>To match you with suitable support workers and deliver your supports safely.</li>
              <li>To claim payment from the NDIA or your plan manager.</li>
              <li>
                To meet our legal duties, for example under the <em>National Disability Insurance Scheme Act 2013</em> (Cth),
                the NDIS Practice Standards and the NDIS Code of Conduct.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">4. Can I stay anonymous?</h2>
            <p>
              You can ask us general questions without giving your name. To provide NDIS supports, we need to know who you
              are.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">5. Who we share it with</h2>
            <p>We only share your information when you agree, or when the law requires or allows it. This can include:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
              <li>the National Disability Insurance Agency (NDIA) and your plan manager, to arrange and pay for supports;</li>
              <li>your support coordinator, nominee or guardian, if you have one;</li>
              <li>health professionals involved in your care, with your consent;</li>
              <li>
                the NDIS Quality and Safeguards Commission, for example when we must report an incident or during an audit;
              </li>
              <li>police or emergency services, if someone is at serious risk;</li>
              <li>services that help us run our business, such as email and record-keeping systems, under confidentiality.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              Some of these services may store information outside Australia. If they do, we take reasonable steps to make
              sure your information is protected in line with the APPs.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">6. How we keep it safe</h2>
            <p>
              We take reasonable steps to protect your information from misuse, loss and unauthorised access. Only people
              who need your information to support you can see it. We keep records for as long as the law requires, then
              destroy them securely.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">7. Seeing and correcting your information</h2>
            <p>
              You can ask to see the information we hold about you, and ask us to correct it if it is wrong or out of date.
              Contact us using the details below. We will reply within 30 days. If we cannot give you access, we will tell
              you why in writing.
            </p>
            <p>
              Because we hold health information in New South Wales, the <em>Health Records and Information Privacy Act 2002</em>
              (NSW) may also apply.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-900">8. Questions and complaints</h2>
            <p>If you have a question or a complaint about your privacy, please contact our Privacy Officer:</p>
            <div class="p-5 rounded-[12px] bg-surface-tint border border-green-200 space-y-1">
              <p class="font-bold text-green-900">Privacy Officer, {SITE.legalName}</p>
              <p>Email: <a href={SITE.emailHref} class={linkClass}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
              <p>Phone: <a href={SITE.phoneHref} class={linkClass}>{SITE.phone}</a> or <a href={SITE.phone2Href} class={linkClass}>{SITE.phone2}</a></p>
              <p>Address: {SITE.streetAddress}, {SITE.suburb} {SITE.state} {SITE.postcode}</p>
            </div>
            <p>
              We will look into your complaint and reply within 30 days. If you are not happy with our answer, you can
              complain to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC): call
              <a href={SITE.oaicPhoneHref} class={linkClass}>{SITE.oaicPhone}</a> or visit
              <a href={SITE.oaicComplaintsUrl} class={linkClass} rel="noopener">the OAIC privacy complaints page</a>.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <HelpContacts />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
